From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Trieloff <lars@trieloff.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:04:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wasi: eza for slicc WASI preview1

eza's Unix code (the long view's permissions, owners, links, inodes,
blocks, --total-size, the inode sort) builds for target_os = "wasi" too,
over src/fs/wasi.rs. WASI's filestat has no mode, owner or block count, and
std::os::wasi::fs is unstable, so that module asks slicc-kernel:

- slicc_fs.path_filestat_owner: the filestat and the owner in one call;
  ENOTSUP with users off, then path_filestat_get and the caller's ids, as
  the kernel reports a file without an owner;
- slicc_fs.path_mode: the permission bits and S_IFIFO; ENOSYS on an old
  kernel, then 0755/0777/0644 by type;
- slicc.cred_get: the caller's ids, for the "you" styles;
- slicc_tty.winsize: the pty's width for the grid (terminal_size has no
  WASI backend).

User and group names come from /etc/passwd and /etc/group, which uzers
(Unix only, through libc) would read. WASI has no device numbers (devices
show no size) or block counts (blocks are the size rounded up to 512).

main() starts in $PWD (wasi-libc starts at /) and, when the kernel
preopened both / and ./ (preopenRoot), closes ./: wasi-libc resolves / to
the last preopen with an empty prefix, which was ./, the working directory.

Signed-off-by: Lars Trieloff <lars@trieloff.net>
